// hello-world-alias.fol — application entry file
// Spec: language-ref.md > Quick Start, `co.*` Paths and Aliases
//
// @co.ddap.alias shortens a co.* path. It is a built-in directive: it is
// self-delimiting and takes no trailing semicolon (DECISION-DIR-001).
// An alias never hides the complete path — both spellings stay valid.

@co.ddap.alias(co.out, as="out")
@co.ddap.alias(co.core.list, as="list")

out.println("Hello FoLang!");

// the complete co.* path remains usable in the same file
co.out.println("Aliases are file-local and additive.");

values := list.of(1, 2, 3);
co.out.println(values);
